  "source": "one-continuous-master",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "At the beach, Pinocchio discovered that the Shark story was a lie.",
      "start": 0.066,
      "end": 4.898
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "His classmates mocked him, and their argument became a violent book fight.",
      "start": 4.898,
      "end": 10.248
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "A heavy schoolbook struck Eugene, leaving him injured on the sand.",
      "start": 10.248,
      "end": 15.133
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "The guilty boys ran away before the officers could question them.",
      "start": 15.133,
      "end": 19.826
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "Because Pinocchio remained beside Eugene, the officers blamed and arrested him.",
      "start": 19.826,
      "end": 25.766
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "He escaped, but the powerful police dog Alidoro chased him into the sea.",
      "start": 25.766,
      "end": 32.118
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "When Alidoro began drowning, Pinocchio turned back and saved his pursuer.",
      "start": 32.118,
      "end": 37.961
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "The dog promised to repay the unexpected act of kindness.",
      "start": 37.961,
      "end": 43.78
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "Soon a Green Fisherman pulled Pinocchio from the water in a net.",
      "start": 43.78,
      "end": 48.123
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "Mistaking him for a rare fish, the cook prepared to fry him.",
      "start": 48.123,
      "end": 53.313
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "Alidoro arrived at the last moment and carried Pinocchio away.",
      "start": 53.313,
      "end": 58.515
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "The rescued puppet finally returned to the Blue Fairy's house.",
      "start": 58.515,
      "end": 64.201
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "A painfully slow Snail left him waiting outside through the night.",
      "start": 64.201,
      "end": 69.425
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "Pinocchio kicked the door, trapped his foot, and regretted his impatience.",
      "start": 69.425,
      "end": 75.859
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "During the following months, he studied, worked, and rebuilt the Fairy's trust.",
      "start": 75.859,
      "end": 82.085
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "At last, she promised that he would wake as a real boy the next day.",
      "start": 82.085,
      "end": 87.6
    }
  ],
